op-devstack: do not use the structured logger for test failures

Before this commit, `TestDemoFail1` would not emit a human-readable
message. This is due to the structured logger escaping all ascii
codes when certain special characters are present (like `=`).

The fix is to not use the structured logger to print test errors.

```go
package pkg

import (
	"testing"

	"github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/op-devstack/devtest"
)

func TestDemoFail1(gt *testing.T) {
	t := devtest.ParallelT(gt)
	t.Require().Equal(
		map[string]int{"a": 1, "b": 2, "c": 3},
		map[string]int{"a": 1, "b": 99, "c": 3},
	)
}

func TestDemoFail2(gt *testing.T) {
	t := devtest.ParallelT(gt)
	t.Require().Equal(1, 2)
}
```

